; DECISIVE BTM-ROOT probe, SumSink branch 1.
; The result (correct $z) is NOT ground, so prefix(e)[5..] = "[2] correct" (9 bytes) is a
; PROPER prefix of the 10-byte result.  Branch 1 calls wz.move_to_path(fixed) with the
; ABSOLUTE `fixed` (it never strips root_prefix_path(), unlike branch 3), so the write lands
; at root ++ fixed = 19 bytes, which re-parses as a DIFFERENT complete expression.
;   double-prefixed => (correct (correct $))
;   root-relative   => (correct $)
(fact a 1)
(fact b 2)
(fact c 3)
(exec 0 (, (fact $k $x)) (O (sum (correct $z) 6 $x)))
